  "scope": "The literal1040-slot caller invokes the actual original-row grid metadata constructor, extracts its returned dimension through real field instructions, restores the original exponent root, and passes the same original row/index and that computed dimension into the indexed lambda machine. The returned raw fraction equals the original lambda with its actual original dimension; no dimension/width/fuel result or selected cost is supplied. Same-run terminal-inclusive physical bounds use original row bits/count, index/exponent lengths and numerical exponent. A separate grid-range theorem derives the actual original grid limit bound from original row widths and proves an original-bit envelope for the same physical run under the explicit exponent-in-grid premise; the later loop must establish this invariant. Index validity, initial input representations/H/A and dense cursor remain supplied. Minimum selection, shifted rows and full guess/solver composition remain separate. Twelve physical cases independently specify exact raw outputs and check both paid bounds.",
